{"spec_element": "ensures",
 "proof_obligation": "bridge",
 "diagnosis": "The second postcondition uses 'i < 1' instead of 'i < 0'. When key is found at position i=0, the early return on line 33 is taken with i=0. Since 0 < 1, the second postcondition requires forall k :: 0 <= k < a.Length ==> a[k] != key, but a[0] == key contradicts this. The correct condition is 'i < 0' so that the two postconditions partition the space: i >= 0 means key was found, i < 0 (i.e. i == -1) means key was not found."}

